<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Grupo Minsa gains $50 mln IFC credit.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Grupo Minsa gains $50 mln IFC credit.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Grupo Minsa SA said on Tuesday that it received an eight-year credit worth $50 million from the International Finance Corp (IFC), a subsidiary of The World Bank.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, IFC will buy Minsa shares worth another $10 million, the corn flour maker said.</p>
<p>Minsa Director General Juan Gargallo said in a statement that the new funds would help the company expand production and to improve its financial position by replacing short-term debt with longer-term debt.</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom (525) 728 9559</p>
